  "N13" [label="(11,1,0) Induction-case: A phase-pure sample of fibrous phosphorus featuring parallel chains of P8 building blocks has been experimentally isolated."];
  "N14" [label="(0,0,0) Induction-common: If multiple theoretical predictions and experimental evidence show P8-based chain structures are stable, then P8-based chains represent a promising structural motif for stable phosphorus allotropes."];
  "N15" [label="(0,0,0) Induction-reasoning: Multiple predictions show P8 chains are stable and experimental isolation confirms this, and if such convergent evidence exists then P8 chains are promising, so P8-based chains represent a promising structural motif for stable phosphorus allotropes."];
  "N16" [label="(12,1,0) Induction-case: Supramolecular chemistry can promote controllable polymerisation of phosphorus chains within nanochannels of porous hosts."];
  "N19" [label="(0,0,0) Induction-common: If multiple different porous host materials successfully stabilize and polymerize phosphorus chains, then confinement in porous hosts is a general strategy for stabilizing novel phosphorus structures."];
  "N21" [label="(15,1,0) Abduction-phenomenon: The structure determination of phosphorus materials in amorphous hosts (like carbon nanotubes) remains elusive."];
  "N22" [label="(0,0,0) Abduction-knowledge: If a host material has high crystallinity, then it enables structural determination by diffraction methods."];
  "N34" [label="(17,1,0) Abduction-phenomenon: Doping MOFs with phosphorus chains of atomic width may improve semiconducting properties of P-MOF composites."];
  "N35" [label="(0,0,0) Abduction-knowledge: If P-MOF composites have improved semiconducting properties, then they address the bandgap challenges of red phosphorus-based materials."];
  "N36" [label="(0,0,0) Abduction-reasoning: P-MOF composites may have improved semiconducting properties, and if such improvement occurs then bandgap challenges are addressed, so P-MOF composites may address the bandgap challenges of phosphorus materials."];
  "N6" [label="(0,0,0) Deduction-rule: If a phosphorus allotrope has instability issues OR requires high energy synthesis OR has unsuitable bandgap, then new phosphorus structures with improved properties are needed."];
  "N9" [label="(10,1,0) Induction-case: Cis-linear chains containing [P8] cages have been predicted to be more stable than P4."];
  "NROOT" [label="(0,0,0) Investigate encapsulation of white phosphorus in the helical channels of the indium-based MOF MFM-300(In) as a crystalline confinement strategy for inducing and stabilising double-helical chains of butterfly P8 units, enabling their crystallographic characterisation and testing their relevance as structural building blocks of amorphous red phosphorus.", fillcolor="lightyellow", style="filled"];
