  "R2" [label="(0,0,0) Reports of phosphorus chain formation in porous host nanochannels and of encapsulated white phosphorus polymerisation in carbon nanotubes provide precedents that confinement in host channels can promote or stabilise phosphorus chain structures."];
  "R3" [label="(0,0,0) Because structural determination of phosphorus materials in amorphous hosts remains elusive, high-crystallinity host materials offer a plausible route for diffraction-based structural determination of confined phosphorus species."];
  "R6" [label="(0,0,0) Because low-nuclearity molecular phosphorus species are highly unstable under ambient conditions, there is a motivation to develop new phosphorus structures with improved properties."];
